fix(panic): never run the install flush on the panic restart path

A userspace panic could not reset: the board parked with a nested panic
instead of a PSCI reset.

    Nested panic detected ... Attempt to take mutex ... with preemption
    disabled @lock_mtx.c:194

panic() disables preemption (osfmk/kern/debug.c), and every call after that
point inherits it.  With kebabkdp=1 removed, 0134 clears panicDebugging, so
the panic reaches kdp_machine_reboot_type() -> PEHaltRestart() ->
KebabPlatformExpert::haltRestart(), which with a live console hands the CPU
to kebab_usb_panic_spin(), the non-returning console pump.  The pump executes
host console commands, and it shared ud_run_reboot_command() with the normal
console thread.  For REBOOT/FASTBOOT/FASTBOOT2 that dispatcher runs
kebab_install_sync_for_reset() from 0148:

    VFS_SYNC(rootvnode->v_mount, MNT_WAIT, vfs_context_current())
    kebab_ufs_sync()  ->  lck_mtx_lock(&kebab_ufs_lock)

MNT_WAIT sleeps on HFS+/UBC/mount locks and the UFS sync takes a mutex, so
the first one to be reached panicked with preemption disabled and the machine
never reset.  Two comments asserted the opposite ("The panic path does not
call this"; "a panic still resets without waiting for a filesystem sync");
nothing enforced it.

Enforce it in three places:

  * ud_run_reboot_command() takes a "panicking" argument.  While panicking a
    reset request is degraded to a plain PSCI SYSTEM_RESET and says so: the
    flush is skipped on purpose, because losing a write that was still queued
    is preferable to never resetting.  Every other command is a diagnostic
    that reaches a driver lock (kebab_touch's ktq.lock, RPMH, SPMI) or
    allocates, so it is refused with one line and the pump keeps running.
  * kebab_install_sync_for_reset() refuses to run when panic_active(), so no
    future caller can reintroduce this.
  * KebabPlatformExpert::haltRestart() sends kPEHaltCPU to PSCI as well once
    panicking, instead of falling through to IODTPlatformExpert's
    shutdown-notification arm (thread_call_allocate(), IORegistryEntry::
    fromPath(), PM clients), which allocates and takes mutexes and is only
    skipped today because a kPEPanicBegin happened to be delivered first.

The console pump itself is unchanged and still lock-free.  Nothing changes
outside a panic: REBOOT/FASTBOOT from the console thread still run the
durable flush before the reset.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/kebab_usb.c b/bsd/dev/kebab_usb.c
--- a/bsd/dev/kebab_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/kebab_usb.c
@@ -1792,16 +1792,52 @@
 	ud.vol_stream = kebab_vol_active();
 }
 
-static void
-ud_run_reboot_command(uint32_t command)
+/*
+ * Console command dispatcher.
+ *
+ * "panicking" is not a hint: the panic console pump (kebab_usb_panic_spin())
+ * calls this with preemption already disabled, inside a panic, on the CPU that
+ * panicked.  Nothing reachable from here in that mode may sleep, take a mutex
+ * or allocate, because any of the three turns the panic into a nested panic --
+ * which is exactly what parked this board with a wedged controller after a
+ * userspace panic.
+ *
+ * The reset commands are the only ones that matter in a panic, and they are
+ * degraded to a plain PSCI SYSTEM_RESET: the durable-install flush is skipped
+ * on purpose.  VFS_SYNC(MNT_WAIT) sleeps on HFS+/UBC/mount locks and
+ * kebab_ufs_sync() takes kebab_ufs_lock before SYNCHRONIZE CACHE, so the flush
+ * is the one thing that must not run here; losing a write that was still queued
+ * is preferable to never resetting.  Every other command is a diagnostic that
+ * reaches a driver lock or allocates, so it is refused with one line and the
+ * pump keeps running.
+ */
+static void
+ud_run_reboot_command(uint32_t command, boolean_t panicking)
 {
+	if (panicking) {
+		if (command == UD_REBOOT_FASTBOOT || command == UD_REBOOT_FASTBOOT2 ||
+		    command == UD_REBOOT_PLAIN) {
+			printf("KEBAB PANIC: reset requested (%s); skipping the install "
+			    "flush (VFS_SYNC and kebab_ufs_lock cannot run with "
+			    "preemption disabled) and resetting via PSCI SYSTEM_RESET\n",
+			    command == UD_REBOOT_FASTBOOT ? "FASTBOOT" :
+			    command == UD_REBOOT_FASTBOOT2 ? "FASTBOOT2" : "REBOOT");
+			/* Does not return on success; prints and keeps the pump alive on
+			 * failure, which is the only safe answer left in a panic. */
+			(void)ud_platform_restart();
+			return;
+		}
+		printf("KEBAB PANIC: command 0x%x refused while panicking; it can "
+		    "sleep or take a mutex, and only a reset is safe here\n", command);
+		return;
+	}
 	/*
 	 * A console-requested reset is the transition from the install phase to
 	 * the next boot.  Make every written byte durable before the PSCI call:
 	 * VFS_SYNC flushes the HFS+ metadata/data still in the UBC and
-	 * SYNCHRONIZE CACHE flushes the drive's write cache.  The panic path
-	 * calls ud_platform_restart() directly (ud_panic_reboot()), so a panic
-	 * still resets without waiting for a filesystem sync.
+	 * SYNCHRONIZE CACHE flushes the drive's write cache.  This is the
+	 * non-panic arm only; the panic pump takes the branch above and never
+	 * waits for a filesystem sync.
 	 */
 	if (command == UD_REBOOT_FASTBOOT || command == UD_REBOOT_FASTBOOT2 ||
 	    command == UD_REBOOT_PLAIN) {
@@ -2150,7 +2186,7 @@
 		}
 		/* Panic/restart only after releasing the transport and acknowledging events. */
 		if (trigger) panic("kebab usb console test");
-		if (command != 0) ud_run_reboot_command(command);
+		if (command != 0) ud_run_reboot_command(command, FALSE);
 		/*
 		 * The installer writes to the root filesystem, which can sleep, so
 		 * it runs here with no transport gate held.  The chunk is still in
@@ -2957,9 +2993,11 @@
 		/*
 		 * A host command is answered outside the transport gate: the restart
 		 * path prints through the same console, and it must not run with
-		 * ud.owner held or with the panic-CPU fence still in the way.
+		 * ud.owner held or with the panic-CPU fence still in the way.  This is
+		 * the panic pump, so the dispatcher gets panicking=TRUE and may only
+		 * reset: no filesystem sync, no driver locks, no allocation.
 		 */
-		if (command != 0) ud_run_reboot_command(command);
+		if (command != 0) ud_run_reboot_command(command, TRUE);
 		/*
 		 * Keep the KDP hand-back from 0099: a debugger that reconnects after
 		 * the panic parks here must not have its 0xFA CONNECT frame eaten as
diff --git a/bsd/dev/kebab_install.c b/bsd/dev/kebab_install.c
--- a/bsd/dev/kebab_install.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/kebab_install.c
@@ -54,6 +54,7 @@
 #include <sys/vnode.h>
 #include <sys/vnode_internal.h>
 #include <kern/clock.h>
+#include <kern/debug.h>
 #include <mach/mach_time.h>
 #include <libkern/libkern.h>
 #include <libkern/crypto/sha2.h>
@@ -977,8 +978,9 @@
 /*
  * Reset-path flush.  FASTBOOT/REBOOT are console commands, so they run after
  * the stream and after any install; the data has to be on the device before
- * the reset, not merely in the UBC or the drive's write cache.  The panic path
- * does not call this: a panic must not wait for a filesystem sync.
+ * the reset, not merely in the UBC or the drive's write cache.  A panic must
+ * not wait for a filesystem sync, and the guard below is what makes that true
+ * instead of a comment that nothing enforces.
  */
 bool
 kebab_install_sync_for_reset(const char *why)
@@ -987,6 +989,21 @@
 	int vfs_error;
 	int dev_error;
 
+	/*
+	 * A panic runs with preemption disabled, so any mutex acquisition on this
+	 * path is an immediate nested panic.  The console command dispatcher used
+	 * to reach this function from the panic pump, which meant a REBOOT from
+	 * the host after a panic ran VFS_SYNC(MNT_WAIT) and then took
+	 * kebab_ufs_lock with preemption disabled.  The dispatcher no longer calls
+	 * this while panicking; this guard keeps the rule true for any future
+	 * caller.
+	 */
+	if (panic_active()) {
+		printf("KEBAB SYNC: %s refused: a panic may not run a filesystem "
+		    "sync (VFS_SYNC/kebab_ufs_lock would nest)\n", why);
+		return false;
+	}
+
 	vfs_error = ki_vfs_sync();
 	dev_error = kebab_ufs_sync();
 	if (dev_error == EROFS) {
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/KebabPlatformExpert.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/KebabPlatformExpert.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/KebabPlatformExpert.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/KebabPlatformExpert.cpp
@@ -218,5 +218,18 @@
 		}
 		return kebab_psci_system_reset();
 	}
+	/*
+	 * A halt requested after a panic has nothing left to halt: the other CPUs
+	 * are parked and the console pump is either running or unavailable.
+	 * IODTPlatformExpert::haltRestart(kPEHaltCPU) is the shutdown-notification
+	 * arm -- thread_call_allocate(), IORegistryEntry::fromPath() and
+	 * pmRootDomain->handlePlatformHaltRestart() -- which allocates and takes
+	 * mutexes.  PEHaltRestartInternal() skips it only because a kPEPanicBegin
+	 * was delivered earlier, and a panic restart must not depend on that.
+	 */
+	if (panic_active() && type == kPEHaltCPU) {
+		printf("KEBAB PANIC: halt requested after a panic; rebooting via PSCI SYSTEM_RESET\n");
+		return kebab_psci_system_reset();
+	}
 	return IODTPlatformExpert::haltRestart(type);
 }
